Description: Keel Linux product fabrication framework
 fab builds a product from a plan, an overlay and a set of conf scripts: it
 resolves the plan against an archive, installs it into a chroot, applies
 the overlays and the removelists, and packs the result.
 .
 Everything a caller can see is unchanged from the TurnKey package this one
 replaces: /usr/bin/fab and the fab-chroot, fab-apply-overlay,
 fab-apply-patch, fab-apply-removelist, fab-cpp, fab-install,
 fab-plan-annotate, fab-plan-resolve and fab-query aliases, the makefile
 fragment at /usr/share/fab/product.mk, and the fablib python package. Only
 the Debian package is renamed, so buildtasks, the shared makefiles and
 every recipe keep working without a change.
